{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/azh4mw","slideIndex":2,"text":"Qualitative business case rather than a quantified ROI claim. User states monetary benefits cannot be reliably quantified. Historical development costs are sunk and cannot be counted as future savings. Existing operations effort already included in the annual baseline must not be counted twice. AI provider consumption costs should use consistent demand assumptions across alternatives. Suggested pilot measurements: application onboarding time, internal operating hours, documentation adoption and coverage of required policies. No measured improvement or payback period is asserted."}